🎬 SORA VIDEO PROMPT — CONCEPT 2: SPLIT-REALITY PANIC

Duration: 25 seconds
Style: Hyper-kinetic montage, existential sci-fi horror
Rule Zero: NO STATIC. NO HOLDS. NO ESTABLISHING SHOTS.
Average shot length: 0.6–1.1s
Max shot length: 1.4s
Aspect: 16:9 cinematic
Split-screen: Vertical, asymmetric, dynamic boundary

🔥 AUDIO (CRITICAL – STARTS BEFORE VISUAL)

BGM:
Industrial PHONK @ ~135 BPM
– distorted 808 bass
– metallic percussion
– machine hum drone
– glitch stutters synced to cuts

SFX Palette:
Sub-bass hits (felt, not heard)
HUD chirps + error buzz
Wet organic breathing (creature side)
Low bone-scrape groans (NOT roars)
Rule:
🎵 First bass hit at 0.3s (before visual clarity)

GLOBAL LOCKS
Camera: handheld micro-jitter, real inertia, no float
Physics: everything has mass, drag, latency
Lighting: hard lunar bounce + cold rim from Earth
NO idle motion (no “subtle drifting” cheat language)
Cuts driven by audio transients


⚡ SCENE BREAKDOWN
SCENE 1 (0.0–0.4s)

Split-screen slams on, no fade.
LEFT: Helmet cam snaps into focus mid-motion, HUD elements misaligned.
RIGHT: Macro view of creature’s eyelid sealed shut, skin twitching beneath.

SFX: low sub rumble rising

SCENE 2 (0.4–0.8s)

Eye snaps open violently, iris constricts.
Split boundary fractures for 1 frame.

SFX: 808 impact + wet membrane pop

SCENE 3 (0.8–1.6s)

LEFT: Astronaut pivots, boot skids on dust, camera lurches.
RIGHT: Eye tracks past the astronaut, not at him.

SFX: boot scrape + distorted breath

SCENE 4 (1.6–2.4s)

LEFT: HUD projects target brackets → brackets drift, fail to lock.
RIGHT: Thin parasite crawls across creature’s cheek, disappearing into flesh seam.

SCENE 5 (2.4–3.2s)

Split tilts diagonally.
LEFT: Laser grid scans ground, slicing dust plumes.
RIGHT: Spines flex independently, casting jagged shadows.

SCENE 6 (3.2–4.0s)

LEFT: Smash zoom-out reveals astronaut tiny vs structures.
RIGHT: Eye remains tight → scale conflict.

SCENE 7 (4.0–4.8s)

RIGHT: Pull back reveals full towering creature, multiple embedded faces blinking asynchronously.
LEFT: HUD floods with MASS UNKNOWN warnings.

SCENE 8 (4.8–5.6s)

Blue jelly entities push up through regolith, ground cracking.
Camera dips to follow emergence.

SFX: wet suction + bass wobble

SCENE 9 (5.6–6.4s)

One jelly entity slides across split boundary, tearing it visually.
HUD whites out for 2 frames.

SCENE 10 (6.4–7.2s)

LEFT: Astronaut stumbles back, regains footing.
RIGHT: Creature’s eye dilates slightly — interest.

SCENE 11 (7.2–8.0s) 🔥

LEFT: Astronaut fires two-round burst, recoil knocks barrel upward.
Laser bolts streak wide, vaporizing dust.
RIGHT: Creature flesh ripples from pressure wave without damage.

SFX: sharp metallic crack + bass slap

SCENE 12 (8.0–8.8s)

Laser impacts a structure → molten fragments explode toward camera.
Jelly entity warps around debris.

SCENE 13 (8.8–9.6s)

RIGHT: Embedded face opens wide, teeth vibrating, no sound emitted.
LEFT: HUD spikes red across visor.

SCENE 14 (9.6–10.4s)

Earth drifts fully into view behind creature’s silhouette, serene.

SCENE 15 (10.4–11.2s)

LEFT: HUD text scrolls uncontrollably, symbols overlapping.
RIGHT: Eye narrows, reflective surface catching Earthlight.

SCENE 16 (11.2–12.0s)

Creature leans forward; mass displaces dust outward.
Astronaut braces instinctively.

SCENE 17 (12.0–12.8s)

Jelly entities duplicate with temporal echo, then recombine.

SCENE 18 (12.8–13.6s)

Split straightens perfectly — unnatural calm.

SCENE 19 (13.6–14.4s)

Split collapses into single frame via violent glitch shear.

SCENE 20 (14.4–15.2s)

Shared frame: human, creature, jellies.
Camera orbits, parallax heavy.

SCENE 21 (15.2–16.0s)

Astronaut lowers weapon halfway.
Creature tilts head, studying.

SCENE 22 (16.0–16.8s)

Earth centered behind them, framed like judgment.

SCENE 23 (16.8–17.6s)

Jelly entities freeze mid-motion, as if awaiting command.

SCENE 24 (17.6–18.4s)

Camera pushes toward Earth, tension rising.

SCENE 25 (18.4–19.2s)

Low sub-bass pulses only.
Breathing syncs between human and creature.

SCENE 26 (19.2–20.0s)

Extreme close-up: astronaut visor reflecting creature’s eye.

SCENES 27–28 (20.0–24.5s)
Rapid alternation:
Creature eye
Earth
Jelly forms
Acceleration each cut.

SCENE 28 (24.5–25.0s)
Bass hit. Hard cut.
Screen jitters once with final bass hit.
Hard cut to black.
Ends clean